  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MANITOBA PRAIRIE PARKLAND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this proposed project is to secure breeding habitats that will benefit waterfowl and other wetland dependant birds that also use wintering habitat along the Gulf of Mexico coast of the United States. Using fee simple acquisition and perpetual conservation easements, the securement of 500 total habitat acres will provide perpetual protection of breeding habitat for populations of 16 priority species that are known to winter in the Gulf region.</narrative>
  </description>
